  book_title: Small-Town Conversations
  book_color: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
  book_clue_index: 108
  content: "This book collects scattered local reporters\u2019 interviews with residents."
  clue_content: "In a section featuring local painters, an unnamed woman talks about
    her unhappy early life. She left her rain-soaked hometown for this remote, sunlit
    little city. She had spent her life painting sunsets, and after hearing that
    the eastern mountains offered the finest views, she rode her bicycle there to
    see for herself.\n\u201CIf I could,\u201D she said, \u201CI would love to dive
    into and touch such radiant sunlight one day.\u201D"
